1
00:00:00,543 --> 00:00:03,447
For small online merchants, a chargeback starts

2
00:00:03,447 --> 00:00:05,231
a race to assemble records.

3
00:00:05,660 --> 00:00:09,202
The order, delivery history, customer messages, and

4
00:00:09,215 --> 00:00:11,728
response policy sit in different places.

5
00:00:12,119 --> 00:00:15,127
Rebuttal brings those records together, recommends a

6
00:00:15,127 --> 00:00:18,004
response, and drafts evidence for review.

7
00:00:18,421 --> 00:00:21,429
The goal is less manual case assembly,

8
00:00:21,832 --> 00:00:24,580
with the merchant retaining control of consequential

9
00:00:24,593 --> 00:00:25,348
decisions.

10
00:00:27,445 --> 00:00:31,416
Rebuttal uses the AWS Strands Agents SDK.

11
00:00:31,833 --> 00:00:35,231
After intake, four agents collect evidence in

12
00:00:35,231 --> 00:00:35,869
parallel.

13
00:00:36,286 --> 00:00:38,408
Strategy waits for all four.

14
00:00:38,825 --> 00:00:41,794
The drafter then receives both the evidence

15
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:43,343
and the proposed response.

16
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:46,208
A separate executor uses an approval hook

17
00:00:46,455 --> 00:00:48,317
before taking a guarded action.

18
00:00:50,451 --> 00:00:52,716
The next scenes replay a recorded local

19
00:00:52,716 --> 00:00:53,029
run.

20
00:00:53,458 --> 00:00:55,789
The merchant records are synthetic, and the

21
00:00:55,789 --> 00:00:57,586
Stripe objects are in test mode.

22
00:00:58,003 --> 00:01:00,242
The screen is an edited presentation of

23
00:01:00,255 --> 00:01:03,237
captured output, so reveals follow the narration

24
00:01:03,393 --> 00:01:05,294
rather than the original wait times.

25
00:01:05,711 --> 00:01:07,768
The owner response comes through the developer

26
00:01:07,781 --> 00:01:08,419
command line.

27
00:01:10,537 --> 00:01:12,855
The recorded run begins with a Stripe

28
00:01:12,855 --> 00:01:13,649
test dispute.

29
00:01:14,079 --> 00:01:16,644
The panel shows selected facts retrieved for

30
00:01:16,644 --> 00:01:20,082
that case: the order, delivery record, customer

31
00:01:20,082 --> 00:01:22,178
communications, and merchant policy.

32
00:01:22,595 --> 00:01:25,511
The execution trace shows the Strands graph

33
00:01:25,524 --> 00:01:28,975
moving through collection, strategy, and drafting.

34
00:01:29,379 --> 00:01:31,384
These excerpts come from the captured local

35
00:01:31,384 --> 00:01:31,748
run.

36
00:01:33,824 --> 00:01:36,481
Next, compare the proposed strategy with the

37
00:01:36,481 --> 00:01:37,861
records that support it.

38
00:01:38,291 --> 00:01:41,611
The recommendation and draft are shown separately.

39
00:01:42,015 --> 00:01:45,140
Read the evidence excerpt alongside the retrieved

40
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:45,791
facts.

41
00:01:46,207 --> 00:01:50,218
Missing evidence and uncertainty must remain visible,

42
00:01:50,647 --> 00:01:52,965
and a proposed action must stay distinct

43
00:01:52,978 --> 00:01:54,137
from a completed action.

44
00:01:56,237 --> 00:01:58,490
The approval step is a deliberate decision

45
00:01:58,490 --> 00:01:58,920
point.

46
00:01:59,323 --> 00:02:02,045
In this recording, the developer command line

47
00:02:02,214 --> 00:02:04,193
stands in for the merchant interface.

48
00:02:04,662 --> 00:02:07,657
Fight, concede, and hold are the three

49
00:02:07,748 --> 00:02:08,959
available responses.

50
00:02:09,376 --> 00:02:11,459
The selected response is passed back to

51
00:02:11,459 --> 00:02:14,441
the Strands interrupt, after which the recorder

52
00:02:14,441 --> 00:02:15,378
checks Stripe again.

53
00:02:15,834 --> 00:02:18,959
Phone notification delivery is disabled for this

54
00:02:18,972 --> 00:02:20,183
local demonstration.

55
00:02:22,284 --> 00:02:24,628
Here is the approval interrupt and the

56
00:02:24,628 --> 00:02:26,438
developer command line response.

57
00:02:26,867 --> 00:02:29,419
The display preserves the recorded choice and

58
00:02:29,419 --> 00:02:30,565
the guarded action count.

59
00:02:30,982 --> 00:02:33,990
After resuming, the recorder reads Stripe again.

60
00:02:34,380 --> 00:02:36,529
Compare the before and after states.

61
00:02:36,958 --> 00:02:40,070
That readback establishes the test result, not

62
00:02:40,070 --> 00:02:42,023
a real-world dispute outcome.

63
00:02:44,137 --> 00:02:47,406
The validation panel identifies the source revision

64
00:02:47,575 --> 00:02:49,190
and the checks that ran against it.

65
00:02:49,606 --> 00:02:52,015
It shows the unit test result alongside

66
00:02:52,015 --> 00:02:56,455
the fixed synthetic-case evaluation, covering action, approval,

67
00:02:56,729 --> 00:02:58,578
expected value, and grounding.

68
00:02:58,981 --> 00:03:02,328
Read the observed results and thresholds together.

69
00:03:02,757 --> 00:03:05,791
This benchmark does not measure real merchant

70
00:03:05,791 --> 00:03:06,872
recovery rates.

71
00:03:08,958 --> 00:03:11,132
Rebuttal gives small merchants a place to

72
00:03:11,132 --> 00:03:14,583
review the facts, the proposed response, and

73
00:03:14,583 --> 00:03:15,390
the next action.

74
00:03:15,807 --> 00:03:18,815
This prototype runs locally with synthetic merchant

75
00:03:18,828 --> 00:03:21,067
data and Stripe test objects.

76
00:03:21,471 --> 00:03:24,440
Real merchant outcomes and live phone delivery

77
00:03:24,765 --> 00:03:26,992
remain outside this demonstration.

78
00:03:27,421 --> 00:03:29,856
The goal is a clearer, more controlled

79
00:03:29,869 --> 00:03:31,041
dispute workflow.
